WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.757
EXPLAIN shows how PostgreSQL plans to execute the statement.

00:00:03.757 --> 00:00:09.382
The purpose here is not to memorize every plan node.

00:00:09.382 --> 00:00:12.457
It is to build the habit of checking instead of guessing.

00:00:12.457 --> 00:00:18.822
On real workloads, data volume, indexes, statistics, and PostgreSQL version all affect the plan.

00:00:18.822 --> 00:00:25.752
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:25.752 --> 00:00:33.652
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a

00:00:33.652 --> 00:00:41.170
new block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
